=== SIGNATURE ===
z_arrow_to_num(x)

=== COMMENT ===
Helper: if x is one of the 8 standard direction arrows, return its numeric-address delta (up -1000000, down 1000000, left -1, right 1, and the four diagonals); anything else (numbers, other text) passes through unchanged.

=== CODE ===
=LAMBDA(x, LET(
   arrows, "↑↓←→↖↗↙↘",
   nums, {-1000000; 1000000; -1; 1; -1000001; -999999; 999999; 1000001},
   i, IFERROR(XMATCH(x, MID(arrows, SEQUENCE(8), 1)), 0),
   IF(AND(ISTEXT(x), i >= 1), INDEX(nums, i), x)
))

=== DESCRIPTION ===
Maps a standard direction arrow to the numeric-address delta you add to a packed address (1e6*row+col) to move one cell that way.

Arguments:
  x - any value. If it is one of the 8 standard arrows the delta is returned; otherwise x is returned unchanged.

Mapping:
  up -1000000, down 1000000, left -1, right 1, up-left -1000001, up-right -999999, down-left 999999, down-right 1000001.

Returns:
  The numeric delta for a standard arrow, else x unchanged. Used to let arrow-taking lambdas accept either an arrow or its number, and by num_ad to convert arrows.

Example:
  z_arrow_to_num("→")   ->  1
  z_arrow_to_num("↘")   ->  1000001
  z_arrow_to_num("hi")  ->  "hi"
